{"id":"resp_91318558f6db1302","created_at":1795618183,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_8b54dbbea4cdf5d7","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce a SHACL shapes graph representing the requirement. The requirement: TRF-036 clause 4.2.1 defines hi (level ice thickness) and h (design ice load height) for each ice class. We have an ice class design parameter set class, with properties: levelIceThickness and designIceLoadHeight. The relationship from ship to its ice class design parameter set via hasIceClassDesignParameterSet. The ownership mapping: designIceLoadHeight and levelIceThickness have owners iceClassDesignParameterSet per termOwners. Also iceClassDesignParameterSet has owner iceClassDesignParameterSet (self). So we need shapes targeting iceClassDesignParameterSet class, requiring properties has levelIceThickness and designIceLoadHeight with appropriate datatype (numericValue) and unit M.\n\nWe need to use quantityEncoding numeric and unit predicates: numericValue, unit.\n\nDefine a sh:NodeShape with sh:targetClass = iceClassDesignParameterSet.\n\nAdd sh:property constraints for each property:\n\n- sh:path iceClassDesignParameterSet-levelIceThickness? Actually property IRI is levelIceThickness.\n\nAdd sh:datatype? Since it's a QuantityValue, we need that the value of levelIceThickness is a blank node of type qudt:QuantityValue with numericValue and unit. In SHACL we can enforce structure: valueNode must be a blank node of type qudt:QuantityValue, with sh:property for numericValue and unit. Simpler: require that the property points to a node that has numericValue of xsd:decimal and unit = M.\n\nThus define a shape for QuantityValue? Could embed within property constraints using sh:node.\n\nDefine a shape \"QuantityValueShape\" targeting qudt:QuantityValue with constraints: sh:property for numericValue with datatype xsd:decimal, and sh:property for unit with sh:hasValue = http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M (maybe enforce exact unit? but maybe allow any unit but recommended unit is M). Since requirement states unit M. So we enforce that unit = M.\n\nThus create a shape for QuantityValue with sh:property on numericValue mandatory, and unit must have value M.\n\nThen for each property path levelIceThickness and designIceLoadHeight, we do sh:node = :QuantityValueShape.\n\nAlso values appear as per table; but no need to enumerate values, just ensure that they are present and have correct unit, maybe also range? Could add sh:minCount 1, maxCount 1.\n\nImplement.\n\nUse prefixes: nltl for ontology.\n\nProvide sh:targetClass.\n\nAll IRIs must be exact canonical.\n\nThus produce Turtle with prefixes: sh, xsd, qudt, nltl.\n\nAdd shapes.\n\nReturn <BEGIN_SHACL> line then turtle then <END_SHACL>.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_bd58716a8b978882","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# Shape that validates a QUDT QuantityValue\n_:QuantityValueShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:M ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n    ] .\n\n# Shape for Ice Class Design Parameter Set\nnltl:IceClassDesignParameterSetShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:iceClassDesignParameterSet ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:levelIceThickness ;\n        sh:node _:QuantityValueShape ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Level ice thickness (hi) for the ice class.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:designIceLoadHeight ;\n        sh:node _:QuantityValueShape ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Design ice load height (h) for the ice class.\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":62627,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":62032,"input_tokens_per_turn":[62627],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":954,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":572,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[954],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":63581},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}